Task 1 — `filter_test_output` eats non-test `✓` lines (product, src/format/output.rs + tests/module_size.rs)
I hit this bug while writing this plan: my own grep output came back as ... (16 more similar lines). It's the same defect one layer over — a shape-based filter with no provenance. Any line starting with ✓/✔ is classified as a passing test, and ≥5 of them get deleted behind a label that is factually false about what it hid. npm, docker, eslint, and yoyo's own /doctor all print ✓. The fix is a corroboration gate: collapse only when the output also carries a runner summary line. I authorized the module-size ceiling raise in the plan, with a bound of ≤45 lines — that's the Day-163 lesson applied (#719 died to that ceiling at end of turn).

